    "title": "Educator of the Week: Mr. Haury of Lincoln Elementary School - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Briana Byus ,\n2 hours ago\nCLOVIS, Calif. ( KSEE ) – Every fall for 18 years, third-grade Lincoln Elementary teacher Micah Haury has worn the same shirt and tie for picture day.\nHis outfit is not the only timeless element of his class, though.\n“My son Alex is now a senior in high school, and he had Mr. Haury in the third grade,” Lincoln Elementary GIS Rachelle Pirok said. “He still sings the math songs. He’s well known for teaching math facts, and he still utilizes that strategy.”\nHaury says his job is about much more than math, though; it’s about helping each child develop as a person.\n“I’m teaching them character, teaching you how to interact with others and just become good citizens and good people,” Haury said.\nPart of helping them become good people, he says, is helping them to discover good role models.\n“In our classroom, we have a wall in the back that we call our Alpha Hawk. An Alpha Hawk is just somebody who lives for others,” Haury said. “There’s many different figures up there, like Martin Luther King Jr., or there’s a lot of parents, there’s siblings, there’s lots of people that we can really look up to and we want to be like.”\nNot every lesson sounds as exciting as an ‘Alpha Hawk,’ though. Sometimes you have to learn sentence structure instead. However, Principal Anisha Mayberry says Mr. Haury can make any topic engaging.\n“They look at him, and they’re ready to learn and just eager. The eagerness that I see in them, I just – I love that,” Mayberry said.\nWhile curricula change and technology advances, some things, like Mr. Haury and his picture day outfit, are consistent.\nIt’s his consistent care for his students that makes him KSEE24’s Educator of the Week.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.",
